    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "`check_password` is implemented in `solution.py` according to `spec.md`, and all 8 tests in `tests/test_solution.py` pass. I haven't seen the coverage, CRAP, mutation or bandit results, because I only ran the pytest command.\n\nIt raises `TypeError` for non-string inputs. Otherwise it checks the five rules (LENGTH, CLASSES, USERNAME, REPEAT, BLOCKLIST) in that order and returns the codes of the ones violated. The tests cover the boundary cases for each rule: length 11, 12, 64 and 65, class counts, the username-length cutoff, case-sensitive repeats, and blocklist equality versus containment. They also cover a password that violates all five rules at once.\n\nMy first test run had two failures, both mistakes in my tests rather than in `solution.py`. I corrected the two test inputs and the suite then passed.",
